ZSNES desktop audio
===================

The audio regression reported on Ubuntu 24.04 for ZSNES 2.3.4 was no
longer reproducible with 2.3.9. The default desktop launcher therefore
uses automatic audio backend selection again.

The package provides four desktop launchers:

  ZSNES           zsnes
  ZSNES (PipeWire) zsnes -ad pipewire
  ZSNES (SDL3)     zsnes -ad sdl
  ZSNES (libao)    zsnes -ad ao

The default backend selection tries native PipeWire first and falls
back to SDL3. The SDL3 and libao launchers let their respective
libraries select the audio driver or plugin automatically.

Advanced troubleshooting
------------------------

Individual audio drivers can be selected from a terminal, for example:

  SDL_AUDIO_DRIVER=pipewire zsnes -ad sdl
  SDL_AUDIO_DRIVER=pulseaudio zsnes -ad sdl
  SDL_AUDIO_DRIVER=alsa zsnes -ad sdl
  zsnes -ad ao:pulse
  zsnes -ad ao:alsa

Other drivers, such as sndio, JACK, OSS or NAS, may be available
depending on the installed SDL3 or libao build. They can be selected
using SDL_AUDIO_DRIVER or -ad ao:<name> as appropriate. See
zsnes --help for the available live libao plugins.

Explicit drivers require a corresponding library driver or plugin
and a working audio device or server. Use the default launcher for
normal play. Only the default launcher registers ROM MIME types.

Regression report: https://github.com/xyproto/zsnes/issues/79
